  "published": "2026-04-28T21:39:42.05Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING: PBKDF2 iteration count for the AES key derivation raised from 1,000 to 600,000 (OWASP guidance for SHA-256). Existing Redis entries written by 12.x cannot be decrypted by this version — flush the configured Redis database (or let the keys expire) before upgrading.\n      BREAKING: Removed the non-generic Get(string) from ISessionState, IApplicationState and IApplicationStateUnbound. Use Get<T>(string) with a concrete type. Calling Get<object>(string) for a complex (JSON-serialized) value now throws InvalidOperationException — the previous behaviour silently returned a JsonElement, which was almost never what callers expected.\n\n      Bug fixes:\n      * Application-state Save: the StackExchange.Redis transaction handle was created but never used, so writes were not actually transactional. Removed the dead transaction; all writes remain FireAndForget as before.\n      * Application-state Save: a reused MemoryStream was reset with Position=0 instead of SetLength(0), causing trailing bytes from a previous (longer) value to leak into the encrypted blob of a subsequent (shorter) value.\n      * Session-state Load: the decompressed MemoryStream used for Brotli payloads was never disposed.\n      * KeyCrypto.Encrypt: rented ArrayPool buffer could leak on exception paths. Now wrapped in try/finally.\n\n      Improvements:\n      * Removed redundant dictionary lookups in Get<T> on ISessionState and IApplicationState.\n      * Removed pointless ArrayPool rent/return in ReadKeyValuePairs (the rented buffer was always copied into a new array anyway).\n      * WriteLengthPrefixedUtfString: corrected off-by-four threshold that could allocate slightly past the stack budget for strings near the boundary.\n      * Application-state Save now scans the dictionary once instead of four times.\n      * FileVersion is now in sync with PackageVersion.\n\n      https://buymeacoffee.com/egbert\n      Source Code available on request.",
